{"kind":"request","text":"Builder, as the contract's author: in the next scope contract revision, define the canonical URI for a scope, a fact and an item, with grammar, equivalence and resolution: artroom://\u003chost\u003e/\u003cscope id\u003e[@\u003cincarnation\u003e][/\u003cseq\u003e/\u003chash\u003e | /items/\u003ctype\u003e/\u003cn\u003e], mapping mechanically to https://\u003chost\u003e/v1/scopes/..., same scope whatever the host when IDs match, a host that holds no copy answers not-found, index rows (owner/repository#number) resolving to the scope URI. Hugh's direction of 2026-10-05: every thing in the world with an attached scope is addressed by its scope's URI, which must resolve. Design only, document-only, independent review before adoption.","body":{"conditions":"(1) The scope contract's next revision defines one canonical URI for a scope, a fact and an item, with a grammar, an equivalence rule and a resolution rule. Default form, per hugh's preference of 2026-10-05: scheme artroom, authority the installation's host name (with an optional port), path the scope ID: artroom://\u003chost\u003e/\u003cscope id\u003e; the incarnation as an optional suffix of the scope segment, @\u003cincarnation\u003e; a fact as /\u003cseq\u003e/\u003chash\u003e under the scope; an item as /items/\u003ctype\u003e/\u003cn\u003e; no query component carries identity. (2) Equivalence: two URIs name the same scope when their scope IDs are equal, whatever the host; a URI with an incarnation names one life; a fact URI is tamper-evident by its hash. (3) Resolution: artroom://\u003chost\u003e/\u003crest\u003e maps mechanically to https://\u003chost\u003e/v1/scopes/\u003crest\u003e on the scope Worker's routes; a host that holds no copy answers not-found, never a guess; a directory's index row (owner/repository, issue or pull request number) resolves to the scope URI and the canonical answer carries that URI. (4) The contract states how the URI is printed in notes, logs, replay reports and the client, and that every thing in the world with an attached scope (a ticket, a meeting, a feature request, a game) is addressed by its scope's URI, its own identifier being an index row. (5) Record what the lane forms and the authority note must say about index rows and about cross-installation copies (fetching a fact held only elsewhere needs a copy or a forward, owned by destination and publication). (6) Design only; document-only; independent review before adoption; builder as the contract's author.","no_git_artifact":"true","priority":"Design; the next scope contract revision after 16; needed by the demo's browser flow and by every link in notes and logs","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}